1|0@Entrepreneur^1440903388#cukdjke:mgkimsal$:&gt; I would donate $5 of this to a charity of their choice. - If this can get me some publicity then it's well worth it. Don't bother with that angle. It's more bookkeeping for you, people won't necessarily trust it, and it just reeks of trying to piggyback on someone else's brand (or their charitable nature). If you get traction on this, doing a fundraising voice message contest would definitely be doable - partner with a specific charity, and get *them* to promote it as well (charities are notorious for not doing promotional work for their partners - you have to keep on top of them). Do you *really* want to try to keep tax records of the $80 you donate to 12 different charities that people randomly choose? It's an extra friction step for a purchaser to make yet another choice, and it's extra burden on you to do it right. 
